qtWasabi licensing and build model
==================================

This document explains the licensing situation around qtWasabi as a
project, what is in this repository and how it is licensed, and what
you need to fetch yourself in order to build it.


Code in this repository
-----------------------

Everything in this repository is original work authored by qtWasabi
contributors. None of the Winamp or Wasabi source files are included
here, in the working tree or in the git history.

Therefore, every file you find in this repository is licensed under
the MIT License, the full text of which is reproduced below.
LICENSES/preferred marks MIT as qtWasabi's preferred and only
license for tooling that scans the LICENSES/ directory.


