Code that is NOT in this repository
-----------------------------------

qtWasabi exists to embed Winamp's Maki bytecode VM and a small
portable subset of Wasabi's foundation classes (BFC) into a Qt6
application. Those pieces are not included in this repository.

In 2024 the Llama Group officially open-sourced the Winamp client and
the Wasabi widget framework. The release is a public source archive
that anyone can download and use under the terms shipped with it. To
build qtWasabi you fetch that release locally and link the relevant
parts into the build.

Why everyone has to build it themselves:

  1. Run scripts/fetch-wasabi.sh. The script downloads the official
     Winamp open-source release into wasabi-src/, a directory that is
     gitignored and never pushed back to this repository.
  2. The build links the open-sourced Winamp pieces (the Maki VM and
     a portable subset of BFC) into the qtWasabi library on your
     local machine.
  3. The licence governing those linked-in Winamp pieces is whichever
     licence the Llama Group ships with the official source release.
     Read the LICENSE.md file inside that release for the exact
     terms. Honouring those terms is your responsibility as the
     person doing the build.

This is the same model console emulators use for BIOS files. The
emulator code is freely distributable under its own licence, the
machine-specific files come from the user.


Why this split
--------------

Two reasons.

First, it keeps qtWasabi cleanly MIT-licensed. Embedders can drop the
qtWasabi library into a Qt media player without inheriting any extra
licence obligations from the original Winamp code.

Second, when the official Winamp repository is back online and
accepting contributions, the qtWasabi code is upstreamable as a Qt
front-end for Wasabi without re-licensing surgery. Everything in
this repository is original work, so the upstream maintainers can
take it in under whatever licence they prefer.


Summary
-------

  qtWasabi (this repository)
      MIT, full text reproduced above. Also mirrored in
      LICENSES/preferred for SPDX-style tooling.

  Maki VM and BFC subset
      Official Winamp open-source release, fetched at build time via
      scripts/fetch-wasabi.sh, governed by the licence shipped with
      that release.

  No Winamp or Wasabi source in this repository or its git history.
